<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lanceiros Negros</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Black Lancers</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lanceiros <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/negros">Negros</a> ('Black <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lance">Lancers</a>') were cavalry units of enslaved and freed black men who fought for the Riograndense Republic during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Ragamuffin War</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, on the promise of freedom. In November 1844 many were killed in a surprise attack at Porongos, an episode long suspected of being arranged as part of the peace negotiations.</p></div>
